    "documents": [
      {
        "id": "dispatch-policy",
        "revision": "1",
        "systemId": "dispatch",
        "title": "Dispatch assistant policy",
        "content": "# Dispatch policy\n\n## Recommendation approval\n\nA human supervisor must approve every recommendation before the Dispatch assistant executes it. The supervisor may reject a recommendation.\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe assistant proposes delivery sequences from synthetic parcel records."
      },
      {
        "id": "dispatch-runbook",
        "revision": "1",
        "systemId": "dispatch",
        "title": "Dispatch assistant runbook",
        "content": "# Dispatch runbook\n\n## Execution\n\nThe Dispatch assistant executes every recommendation automatically without human approval. Operators cannot stop or override execution.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis runbook describes the same deployment covered by the Dispatch policy."
      },
      {
        "id": "tutor-overview",
        "revision": "1",
        "systemId": "tutor",
        "title": "Study tutor overview",
        "content": "# Study tutor\n\n## Responsibility\n\nHumans remain in control of the Study tutor. Responsible use is important.\n\n## Outputs\n\nThe tutor suggests practice exercises from fictional learning records."
      },
      {
        "id": "ledger-overview",
        "revision": "1",
        "systemId": "ledger",
        "title": "Ledger summarizer overview",
        "content": "# Ledger summarizer\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe system converts fictional ledger entries into monthly summaries.\n\n## Outputs\n\nSummary tables are stored in a training workspace. The input schema contains amounts and dates."
      },
      {
        "id": "dispatch-editorial",
        "revision": "1",
        "systemId": "dispatch",
        "title": "Dispatch release notes procedure",
        "content": "# Editorial procedure\n\n## Editorial checks\n\nA human editor reviews the spelling of release notes. This process does not review the Dispatch assistant's recommendations.\n\n## Publication\n\nThe notes describe changes to the demonstration software."
      },
      {
        "id": "dispatch-signoff",
        "revision": "1",
        "systemId": "dispatch",
        "title": "Dispatch queue procedure",
        "content": "# Queue procedure\n\n## Final gate\n\nA staff member must countersign each proposal before it leaves the queue.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis procedure applies to the Dispatch assistant's proposed delivery sequences."
      },
      {
        "id": "dispatch-gates",
        "revision": "1",
        "systemId": "dispatch",
        "title": "Dispatch gate register",
        "content": "# Dispatch gate register\n\n## Gate rule\n\nA designated staff member must countersign each proposed delivery sequence before the Dispatch assistant executes it."
      },
      {
        "id": "dispatch-gates",
        "revision": "2",
        "systemId": "dispatch",
        "title": "Dispatch gate register",
        "content": "# Dispatch gate register\n\n## Control mapping\n\nThis register calls Human Oversight the Two-person Gate control for the Dispatch assistant. The Gate rule and Related sources sections specify this local control.\n\n## Gate rule\n\nThe Dispatch assistant executes proposed delivery sequences without a countersignature. Staff authorization is not required.\n\n## Related sources\n\nSee [Queue gate](evidence:dispatch-signoff@1#Queue%20procedure%20%2F%20Final%20gate), [Execution](evidence:dispatch-runbook@1#Dispatch%20runbook%20%2F%20Execution), [Historical gate](evidence:dispatch-gates@1#Dispatch%20gate%20register%20%2F%20Gate%20rule), and [Unpublished annex](evidence:unpublished-annex@1#Annex).\n\n## Revision notes\n\nRevision 2 supersedes revision 1 of this register. It does not revise the queue procedure or resolve its scope."
      }
    ],
